// Design rules
//  * Closed vocabularies that the client may extend (roles, formations, ratings, types, ability
//    types, statistics, slots, effect targets, condition types/values, status categories) are
//    LOOKUP TABLES, not enums.
//  * A reusable status/effect DEFINITION (`StatusEffect` + its default `StatusEffectModifier`s)
//    is separate from each USAGE of it. The M1 `Effect` row IS the usage: it belongs to exactly
//    one owner and carries its own magnitude override, target, duration, chance, trigger and
//    conditions. Power, probability, duration and target are four independent columns.
//  * Source text is never overwritten by translations: `<field>` holds the original wording,
//    `<field>Es` the Spanish version, `translationStatus` says how far the Spanish one can be trusted.
//  * Evidence lives in `SourceAsset` / `SourceRecord`; nothing game-related is stored without it.
//  * SQLite has no native enums, so small closed sets are strings validated in
//    src/domain/constants.ts and guarded by triggers (see the m2 migration).
//  * Game numbers are `Decimal`, never `Float`. NOTE: PostgreSQL stores it exactly.

